--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
RISKS & ROLLBACK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
R1  Server family-rule mirror missing -> `fsWriteBinary` unreachable via
    public API (may 409 or map to "system").
    Mitigation: `writeBinary` alias works with zero server change.
    Owner: whoever controls awtsmoos.com tunnel control plane.

R2  Tunnel control-plane payload limit smaller than the agent's 16 MB
    BODY_LIMIT (limit unknown — never measured for this route).
    Mitigation: T5 measures it; client chunks conservatively (start 4 MB).

R3  Replay/ledger wrappers (Replay.run, Ledger.record, Provenance) wrap
    every fs action — including the new one — so retries are idempotent
    (same path+content => same bytes). No new double-write hazard beyond
    what `write` already has.

R4  No JS verification on binary path — INTENTIONAL (binary is not JS).
    The secret-path and root guards are unchanged (assertNotSecret,
    safePath), so no new filesystem exposure vs the existing `write`.

R5  Agent restart timing — restart while a transfer is in flight aborts
    it. Mitigation: deploy when no transfer is running; transfers are
    resumable (client re-sends).

ROLLBACK (additive change — nothing existing is modified):
  1. Re-push the 3 backup files from /tmp/bak_* to their original paths.
  2. Restart the agent.
  3. Confirm `writeBinary`/`fsWriteBinary` return unknown-action and the
     manifest hash returns to its previous value.
  The only behavioral delta being reverted is the new RULES entry, which
  previously mapped nothing (no pre-existing `fsWrite*` actions exist).

